                "sender": "w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov",
                "senderName": "NWS Charleston SC",
                "headline": "Special Weather Statement issued November 24 at 12:20AM EST by NWS Charleston SC",
                "description": "Areas of fog will impact much of Colleton, Charleston, Berkeley and\nDorchester Counties through 5 AM. The fog could become locally dense\nat time with visibilities dropping to 1/4 mile or less. The nature of\nthe fog is such that visibilities will vary greatly over short\ndistances with the risk for locally dense fog being the greatest near\nbodies of water and other low-lying areas such as marshes, swamps and\nlarge ditches. Motorists should remain alert for these conditions\nthis morning.\n\nVisibilities are expected to improve prior to daybreak as a cold\nfront drops south through the area.",
                "instruction": "If driving, slow down and leave extra distance ahead of you in case a\nsudden stop is needed.",
