                "description": "Periods of on-and-off light wintry precipitation will continue\nacross the South Plains, Rolling Plains, and far southern Texas\nPanhandle overnight. Initially, precipitation will be a mix of\nsleet, rain, and snow, which is then expected to transition to\nmostly or all snow early Tuesday morning. Sleet and snow\naccumulations, if any, are expected to remain very light with\ntemperatures near or only slightly below freezing. However, a few\nslick spots cannot be ruled out on area roadways, particularly on\nbridges and overpasses. Motorists are encouraged to use extra\ncaution during the morning commute Tuesday. Precipitation will\nthen come to an end by early Tuesday afternoon.",
