                "headline": "Special Weather Statement issued November 23 at 1:38AM CST by NWS Lubbock TX",
                "description": "An approaching storm system late Monday will bring increasing\nmoisture and colder temperatures to the region. Overnight lows are\nexpected to fall below freezing area-wide, allowing for isolated\nto scattered snow showers to develop overnight and continue into\nTuesday morning. Any accumulations are expected to remain light,\nwith little to no impacts anticipated. However, a few slick spots\ncannot be ruled out, particularly on bridges and overpasses.\nMotorists are encouraged to use caution during the morning\ncommute Tuesday.",
